  <main_text>
    <l n="1">sent.) Denique <i>Flauium Clementem</i> pa-</l>
    <l n="2">truelem suum: vix Confulatu perfu-</l>
    <l n="3">nctum, cuius filios paruulos, Imperij</l>
    <l n="4">succeffores, palàm destinauerat ob</l>
    <l n="5">Christianam Religionem, unà cum u-</l>
    <l n="6">xore <i>Flauia Domitilla</i> necandum cura-</l>
    <l n="7">uit. Nec certè dubito, plures ex ipso</l>
    <l n="8">flore nobilitatis, &amp; stirpe Regia, pro</l>
    <l n="9">Christiana religione sub <i>Domitiano</i> oc-</l>
    <l n="10">cisos, quorum nomina ille obliuione</l>
    <l n="11">sepelienda curauit; cùm monumenta</l>
    <l n="12">&amp; gesta Martyrum (quæ <i>Clemens</i> sep-</l>
    <l n="13">tem Notarijs describenda commisit,)</l>
    <l n="14">flammis mandauerat. Ita, ut pro Ge-</l>
    <l n="15">stis Christianorum Martyrum, qui sub</l>
    <l n="16">illo passi, ad Ethnicos Scriptores, qui</l>
    <l n="17">ista subobscure &amp; malitiose consignâ-</l>
    <l n="18">runt, recurrendum sit. Neque tamen</l>
    <l n="19">(vel inimicis atteftantibus) Christiano-</l>
    <l n="20">rum quisquam perduellionis aut læsæ</l>
    <l n="21">maiestatis reus peragitur: cum tamen</l>
    <l n="22">omnium ordinum aliqui iniurijs affecti,</l>
    <l n="23">ad conspirationem contra Impera-</l>
    <l n="24">torem ineundam procliues essent. Se-</l>
    <l n="25">natores oppressi, Philosophi ob lo-</l>
    <l n="26">quendi libertatem expulsi, Iudæi ex</l>
    <l n="27">tribu <i>David</i> interfecti; tributis insuper</l>
  </main_text>
